<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bank  ASLK-CGER 1996 profit rises 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian bank  ASLK-CGER 1996 profit rises 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996</p>
<p>(billions of Belgian francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	   6.82 vs   5.43</p>
<p>    Cons net interest margin		   45.24 vs  37.56</p>
<p>    Commissions received			  6.89 vs   5.39</p>
<p>    Commissions paid				4.53 vs   2.96</p>
<p>    Exchange and trading income		 1.98 vs   1.83</p>
<p>    Capital gains				   2.18 vs   1.98</p>
<p>    Personnel costs				23.92 vs  21.37</p>
<p>    Other operating costs			 8.83 vs   8.03</p>
<p>    Provisions,write offs,write downs	 7.24 vs   7.82</p>
<p>    Fund for general banking risks	    1.00 vs   0.69</p>
<p>    Exceptional charge			    3.06 vs   0.23</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian ASLK-CGER Bank is 49.9 percent owned by Belgian-Dutch insurance and banking group Fortis AMEV.AS. The exceptional result was strongly influenced by the closure of a real estate portfolio in France, ASLK-CGER said in a statement.</p>
</text>
